  "reason": "The current best (config_027, acc=0.706) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted. The only untested variation within this strong sub-space is the aggregation method. Transformer aggregation was tested only with pca_n2000 (config_015, acc=0.586 vs 0.629 for avgpool), where it underperformed. However, scvi_n200 produces a learned, structured latent representation rather than a linear PCA projection, so attention-based aggregation across profiles may extract richer cross-profile interactions that avgpool would average away. This experiment directly tests whether the aggregation choice that was suboptimal for PCA becomes beneficial for the superior scvi_n200 encoder, while keeping all other hyperparameters at their best-known values. Expected cost is moderate (~4.5–5 GPU hours, comparable to config_015 at 4.55 and config_027 at 4.82), making it a low-risk, high-information experiment. If transformer aggregation improves on 0.706, it would set a new best; if not, it confirms avgpool is optimal for scvi_n200 and the remaining budget can focus on other directions."
}

